  "question": {
    "text": "A boy ties a stone of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>100</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math> to the end of a <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math> long string and whirls it around in a horizontal plane. The string can withstand the maximum tension of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>80</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></math>. If the maximum speed with which the stone can revolve is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>K</mi><mi>&#960;</mi></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>rev</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>min</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>. The value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>K</mi></math> is :<br />(Assume the string is massless and un-stretchable)",
    "image": null
  },
